### -----------------------------------------------------------
### Spring AI MCP Client - API Test Requests
### -----------------------------------------------------------
### This file contains HTTP requests for testing the AI chat
### endpoint exposed by the Spring Boot MCP client application.
###
### The endpoint sends prompts to the LLM via Spring AI and
### allows the model to automatically invoke tools exposed
### by the DVaaS MCP server when needed.
### -----------------------------------------------------------


### Health Check
### -----------------------------------------------------------
### Verify that the Spring Boot application is running.
### Expected response: 404 or valid endpoint response depending
### on the available mappings.
GET http://localhost:8080


### Basic Chat Request
### -----------------------------------------------------------
### Sends a prompt to the AI chat endpoint.
### The LLM may call MCP tools from the DVaaS server
### to retrieve up-to-date information about Dan Vega.
###
### Endpoint implemented in ChatController.
GET http://localhost:8080/chat


### Example Dynamic Chat Request (if using @RequestParam)
### -----------------------------------------------------------
### If the controller is updated to accept a dynamic message
### parameter, you can send custom prompts like this.
###
### Example:
### GET /chat?message=What are Dan Vega's latest YouTube videos
GET http://localhost:8080/chat?message=What are Dan Vega's latest YouTube videos


### AI + MCP Tool Invocation Demo
### -----------------------------------------------------------
### This request demonstrates how the LLM can automatically
### call MCP tools exposed by the DVaaS server to enrich
### its response with real-time or external data.
###
### The tool invocation happens transparently through
### Spring AI's ToolCallbackProvider integration.
GET http://localhost:8080/chat?message=Show me Dan Vega's newest content